      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If the majority of the user in the instance doesn't interact or vote \"No\" to the vote kick, the user being voted to be kicked will not be kicked. Vote to kick should always be an option, certain group instance are just made but not moderated, because they can be made by random users. Blocking the functionality would be counterproductive in every way.\n\nWhenever there is a vote kick happening, do not ask the person that did the vote kick. Go look at the person being vote kicked instead, you will most likely see the problem yourself. The only moment you really need to go talk to the person that did the vote kick is whenever the person is literally just standing there and doing nothing interesting.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-01-03T09:30:22.261Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As a group owner It would be a huge advantage to have Vote to kick go to my moderation team before it goes to all of the users in the instance.  This would allow for the group moderators to resolve the issue without notifying every user in the instance of the vote to kick.  This is helpful to keep moderation activities quiet and not disturb the peace of the instance with everyone asking \"why is X person being voted for a kick\"\n\nThe standard vote to kick functionality is very useful in instances where there are no moderators present such as public instances but it draws attention to problems that moderation teams can solve.  The workload on the moderators is actually increased by not only having to deal with the issue but also having to explain to 30 or more people what was going on.",
